<http://data.silknow.org/object/30ca9512-a7d5-30b9-9bba-a70c3ca150fb>
        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Tassel of bright yellow silk. The main body is cylindrical (2.5 inches) topped by a smaller bulbous shape (1.5 inches) with a waist. Core of wood covered with silk. The covering consists of strands of bright yellow twisted silk bound flat, and held down by a yellow silk net, simple twisted lattice over the bulbous part and knotted in a chequer pattern over the cylinder. The fringe is made from a portion of the silk covering falls straight with cut ends, 4 inches long. The base is covered by the rest of the yellow silk strands knotted in the hollow centre of the core."@en , "Tassel of silk, possibly made in France or Italy, 1700-1750"@en ;
        ecrm:P138i_has_representation  <http://data.silknow.org/image/033f31ee-5dcf-32c1-ade8-9626177c11fc> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "Tassel of silk, possibly made in France or Italy, 1700-1750"@en , "Tassel of bright yellow silk. The main body is cylindrical (2.5 inches) topped by a smaller bulbous shape (1.5 inches) with a waist. Core of wood covered with silk. The covering consists of strands of bright yellow twisted silk bound flat, and held down by a yellow silk net, simple twisted lattice over the bulbous part and knotted in a chequer pattern over the cylinder. The fringe is made from a portion of the silk covering falls straight with cut ends, 4 inches long. The base is covered by the rest of the yellow silk strands knotted in the hollow centre of the core."@en ;
